      ":question/problem": "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt} = \\frac{y^{2} - 5 y + 6}{y - 1}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following are equilibrium solutions? Select all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "An equilibrium is a constant function $y(t)=c$. Set $dy/dt=0$ and test the resulting equation.\n\nFirst keep the original domain: $y - 1\\ne0$.\n\nWe need\n\n$$\nf(c) = \\frac{c^{2} - 5 c + 6}{c - 1}=0.\n$$\n\n- For $c=-3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-3) &=- \\frac{15}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is nonzero, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2) &=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is zero, so it is an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3) &=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is zero, so it is an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=1$, $c - 1=0$ violates the original domain, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\nSelect $y=2$ and $y=3$.",
